  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), polled Monday 16 January 1928 in the Town Hall. Nine candidates were nominated for the five seats of the members retiring by rotation (John Hopps, Henry Megarry and others); seven went to the poll. Thirty-six papers were spoilt, some marked in the proportional-representation manner. Party labels are not printed."
